From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:35:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: apple,macaudio: Describe the TDM idle
 properties

macaudio reads two properties for each speaker codec from the dai-link
node, dai-tdm-idle-mode-<n> ("zero" or "pulldown") and
dai-tdm-slot-tx-idle-mask-<n> (a 32-bit slot mask), where <n> is the
position of the codec in the link's codec sound-dai list. It passes them
to the codec's set_tdm_idle(), which sets how the codec drives those
transmit slots while they are idle. The device trees of the speaker
machines set them, but the binding does not describe them, so
dt-validate rejects them and, with no type to go by, fails to decode
their values as well.

Describe both as pattern properties of the dai-link node. A link has at
most eight codecs, so <n> is 0 to 7, and the driver accepts only the two
drive modes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit eb4b28671ec7d360e426a440b4a04a805f1d770e)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
index a80f59e315..fdf3d1883a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
@@ -94,6 +94,24 @@ patternProperties:
         required:
           - sound-dai
 
+    patternProperties:
+      "^dai-tdm-idle-mode-[0-7]$":
+        description: |
+          How the CODEC at this index of the codec sound-dai list drives the
+          TDM transmit slots it leaves idle. The index counts the CODECs of
+          the link in list order, across both CPU-side DAIs.
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+        enum:
+          - zero
+          - pulldown
+
+      "^dai-tdm-slot-tx-idle-mask-[0-7]$":
+        description: |
+          Transmit slots of the CODEC at the same index that are idle and
+          driven as dai-tdm-idle-mode-<n> says, one bit per slot with slot 0
+          in the LSB. Only used together with dai-tdm-idle-mode-<n>.
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+
     required:
       - reg
       - cpu
